  "portableA": {
    "source": ".docs/wiki/kanban.md",
    "heading": "Portable A-card lesson contract",
    "text": "An A card delivers a standalone, browser-openable lesson bundle with a small interactive exercise: choose an action or condition, inspect a synthetic trace, and check the expected outcome. Use standard HTML/browser behavior so an approved application framework or Azure subscription is not needed to begin.\r\n\r\nEach bundle declares source ID, objective, preconditions, actions, synthetic input/trace, expected assertions, and limits. It prominently says **Training rehearsal - synthetic data - not a live Azure result**, makes no management calls, contains no credentials, and supports keyboard operation.\r\n\r\nEach lesson must add a worked, testable exercise rather than copying the backlog sentence. Keep it portable for later mounting by C041. The native implementation and evidence remain a separate B card, and the source demo is not complete until both required slices and its original acceptance gates pass."
  },
